.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt SATLD.TOML 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm satld.toml
.Nd configuration file for the SatL daemon
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the configuration file of
.Xr satld 8 ,
in TOML format.
Every key is optional and a missing file means all defaults, so a fresh
install runs without one.
Unknown keys are rejected at startup: a typo fails loudly instead of
being silently ignored.
The default path is
.Pa /usr/local/etc/satl/satld.toml ,
overridable with
.Ql satld \-\-config .
.Pp
The keys, in the order the daemon declares them:
.Ss socket_path
Path (string).
Default
.Ql /var/run/satl.sock .
Unix socket the Docker REST API is served on.
Change it to run a second daemon on one host, together with
.Ql network_name .
.Ss state_dir
Path (string).
Default
.Ql /var/db/satl .
Node state directory; it should be the mountpoint of
.Ql zfs_root ,
and the daemon warns at startup when the two disagree.
.Ss zfs_root
ZFS dataset name (string).
Default
.Ql zroot/satl .
Root dataset holding all SatL datasets; startup fails when it is
absent, ZFS is mandatory and there is no fallback storage driver.
.Ss node_name
String.
Default: the hostname.
Node name, also shown by
.Ql satl node ls .
.Ss socket_group
Group name (string).
Default
.Ql wheel .
Group owning the REST API socket.
.Ss pf_mode
One of
.Ql enforce ,
.Ql check
or
.Ql disabled
(string).
Default
.Ql check .
How the node-local network manager applies its pf rules:
.Ql enforce
syntax-checks and loads the
.Ql satl/*
anchors,
.Ql check
only syntax-checks the generated rules, and
.Ql disabled
never invokes pfctl at all (hosts without pf).
Published ports need
.Ql enforce :
under the default
.Ql check
mode ports are recorded and shown by
.Ql satl ps
but no redirect is ever installed, which is easy to mistake for a
networking bug.
Never run two daemons in
.Ql enforce
on one host: the
.Ql satl/rdr
anchor is one per host, so each daemon's reconciliation deletes the
other's rules.
.Ss network_name
String, at most 14 characters.
Default
.Ql satl .
Name of the node-local bridge network; it also names the bridge
interface (default
.Ql satl0 )
and the interface group SatL marks and sweeps everything it owns with.
Two daemons on one host must use different names, or each one's
reconciliation destroys the other's interfaces.
.Ss network_pool
IPv4 subnet in CIDR notation (string).
Default
.Ql 10.88.0.0/16 .
Pool the per-network /24 subnets are carved from; change it when it
collides with your underlay.
.Ss egress_if
Interface name (string).
Default: unset, meaning the interface carrying the default route at
startup.
Interface container traffic is NAT-ed out of.
.Ss listen_addr
.Ql host:port
(string).
Default
.Ql 0.0.0.0:2377 .
Address the internal gRPC server (Raft, Control, Dispatcher, NodeCA)
binds.
Every node listens.
The unauthenticated NodeCA bootstrap listener always binds the same
address one port above (default 2378).
.Ss advertise_addr
.Ql host:port
or bare address (string); a bare address gets the listen port appended.
Default: unset, meaning the address of the interface carrying the
default route, which is what an operator would write by hand on an
ordinary host.
Set it explicitly on a multi-homed host, cloud hosts in particular,
where the default route leaves through a public interface while peers
must dial the private underlay: the value is also published as this
node's VXLAN endpoint, so a wrong or missing one makes overlay traffic
go nowhere.
Use an IP literal, not a hostname; a VXLAN endpoint is an address.
.Ss overlay_blackhole
Bare IPv4 address (string).
Default: unset, meaning the last usable host of the measured underlay
prefix (for example
.Ql 10.2.255.254
on a /16).
The blackhole default remote every VTEP is created with; it must be an
address nothing answers on, because
.Xr vxlan 4
sends every broadcast, multicast and unknown-unicast frame there.
Set it only on a fabric that really does use the top address of its
prefix.
.Ss cert_validity
Duration string, an integer with a mandatory unit suffix:
.Ql s ,
.Ql m ,
.Ql h
or
.Ql d
(for example
.Ql 5m ,
.Ql 90d ) .
Default: unset, meaning 90 days, the only production setting.
This is a testing knob for exercising certificate renewal; values below
one hour are issued under a loud startup warning and values below one
minute are refused.
.Ss metrics_addr
.Ql host:port
(string).
Default: unset, meaning the Prometheus
.Ql /metrics
endpoint is off.
The endpoint is unauthenticated, like dockerd's, so pick a private
address; the
.Ql \-\-metrics\-addr
command-line flag wins over this key.
.Ss keyring_rotate_after_secs
Integer seconds.
Default 43200 (12 hours).
Rotation cadence of the encrypted-overlay keyrings.
A testing knob: shortening it makes encrypted networks rotate their
data-plane keys within minutes, under a loud startup warning.
.Ss keyring_phase_settle_secs
Integer seconds.
Default 60.
Settling time between keyring rotation phases; it must be smaller than
.Ql keyring_rotate_after_secs .
A testing knob to shorten together with the rotation interval in tests,
never alone on a real cluster.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/satl/satld.toml.sample
Installed sample listing every key and its default.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A minimal production file, enabling published ports and pinning the
address peers dial on a multi-homed host:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pf_mode = "enforce"
advertise_addr = "10.0.0.11"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr satl 1 ,
.Xr satld 8
